This is the clearest way to cover all wording identified in the conversation without confusing semantic classification with monetary direction.

21. Add value types beyond money, date and text

The label schema currently supports:

money
date
date range
text
regex.

A stronger schema should add:

percentage
identifier
integer
duration
currency
boolean
money pair
money plus date
open date range

These would improve validation for:

interest rates;
statement numbers;
remaining contract terms;
currencies;
combined credit and debit totals;
interest owing as at a date;
START - date periods.

If additional primitive types cannot be added immediately, use constrained regex value types rather than unrestricted text.

22. Make matching longest-first and boundary-aware

The current case-insensitive substring model is useful but too permissive for production extraction.

Matching should follow this order:

exact normalised phrase;
longest token-boundary phrase;
anchored regular expression;
OCR-tolerant phrase;
short fallback label only when value type and layout agree.

Examples requiring longest-first handling include:

current payment due date before payment due;
total minimum payment due before minimum payment;
principal balance before balance;
transaction type and details before type;
opening interest rate before opening;
total of new transactions for before new transactions for.
23. Add context and scope controls

Support constraints beyond where: page1, including:

page 1 only;
first statement page;
outside transaction table;
inside summary region;
inside fee-summary table;
inside loan-summary table;
immediately after label;
same line;
next line;
right of label;
below label;
before transaction table;
group heading only.

This will materially reduce collisions involving words such as balance, payment, date, interest, opening and closing.

24. Add reconciliation-based confidence

A strong extractor should validate results through financial relationships where the document supplies enough evidence.

Examples include:

opening balance, credits, debits and closing balance;
previous balance, payments, purchases and current balance;
page brought-forward and carried-forward values;
transaction balance movement;
page totals and period totals;
loan principal balance continuity.

American Express prints a balance equation across the summary, while ANZ supplies page and period totals and repeated running balances.

Reconciliation should:

increase confidence when values agree;
flag mismatches;
never silently alter extracted values;
identify the likely failing page or row;
retain both printed and calculated results.
25. Add multi-document segmentation

Several supplied PDFs contain multiple statements and other document types in one file. The extractor should segment using combinations of:

document title;
statement number;
account number;
statement period;
opening or closing date;
page numbering reset;
account section heading;
repeated issuer header.

A new statement should begin when strong document-start evidence appears, even when the PDF itself is one file.

This is critical for Amex, ANZ - 9 Columns (4) and ANZ Loan (5), each of which contains multiple pages or statement instances.

