Priority 1: Required for accurate extraction
Separate label, header, structure, direction and transaction-class vocabularies.
Support multiple statements within one PDF.
Support multiple date concepts, including transaction, processed, effective and snapshot dates.
Support single-amount tables using CR/DR suffixes.
Support separate withdrawal and deposit columns.
Support multi-column descriptions without losing intermediate fields.
Add statement, card, customer, membership, loan and facility identifiers.
Add structural group headings, subtotals, page totals and continuation rows.
Add ordinal-date normalisation and year inference.
Add leading minus, trailing minus, parentheses, CR, DR and OD monetary forms.
Add open date ranges such as START - date.
Add reconciliation and confidence scoring.
Remove "test" from closing_balance.
Remove unqualified opening and closing from statement date labels.
Avoid generic substring-only matching.
Priority 2: Required for broad product coverage
Add credit-card payment, credit-limit and amount-payable fields.
Add loan balances, repayments, interest, review dates and maturity fields.
Add account snapshot fields, including frozen and uncleared amounts.
Add foreign-currency details, conversion rates and commissions.
Add percentage and duration value types.
Add transaction-code dictionaries.
Add fee, interest, reversal, adjustment, transfer, payment, tax, cash and loan classes.
Retain valid zero-amount account events.
Classify notices and informational pages separately.
Propagate card, account and section context to following rows.
Priority 3: Production hardening
Add schema versions and migration rules.
Add duplicate and collision validation.
Add conservative OCR normalisation.
Preserve raw text, location, source page and matched wording.
Build a regression suite from every supplied statement family.
Record unmatched high-confidence labels and headers for maintainer review.
Test statement segmentation, row counts, totals and balance continuity.
Final conclusion

The recommendations now cover everything materially identified in this conversation and all supplied statement examples reviewed so far.

The three newest files add the final major structural requirements:

American Express adds membership identifiers, cardholder transaction groups, amount payable, foreign-spending detail, single-amount CR notation and per-cardholder subtotals.
ANZ transaction statements add a combined multi-column description structure, code legends, page and period totals, open-ended statement periods, no-transaction periods and account-level available credit.ANZ loan documents add principal balances, processed dates, loan summaries, principal and interest totals, next-payment fields, rate-review dates, maturity dates, fee-summary tables and rate-change notices.

The result should not be implemented as one enormous flat vocabulary. The production design should be a controlled hierarchy of:

document labels;
table headers;
direction evidence;
transaction classes;
structural rows;
document and section types;
typed values;
reconciliation rules; and
extraction provenance.

That structure gives you complete coverage of the supplied corpus while remaining maintainable when the next unfamiliar bank statement appears.
